    },
    "body": "The previous reader constructed semantic addresses through four dense current/identity q/k maps. This adds an opt-in geometric reader in the existing Rust learned stack: direct signed-2I content/context codes, directed relative actions, learned unary/cross potentials, physical radius and explicit presence, with the four q/k maps removed. Joint language gradients, causal/self/NoRead support, existing capture timing and payload/output interfaces remain integrated. Saved artifacts bind geometry and model identities; incompatible replay/export paths refuse the mode.\n\nBoth fixed320-update seeds answered128/128 original and128/128 longer-gap authored cases with head0 correct-source majorities throughout. Independent reload and ablation restoration are exact. Context-factor ablation reduces answers to13/21 and source majorities to0; readout ablation to4/9. Cross-only removal leaves124/128 each, so the report does not claim standalone cross necessity or group advantage. Raw models/reports remain retained; compact hashes and per-condition evidence are committed.\n\nValidation:10 geometric-address checks,10 retained latch checks,1 ordinary fused gradient reference; cargo fmt --check, claim wording and git diff checks. Actual fit/evaluation522.317s, maximum RSS90.0MiB, no timeout. Mixed float offline prototype: finite-table export, native integer code producer/capture/trunk/value/output, bounded indexing, natural language and energy remain unfinished. Donor-informed geometric compilation remains an explicit supported route.\n\nReferences #1512, #973, #820.\n",
